---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

import Note from '~/components/widgets/Note.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Editorial Policy: How We Update Countdown Dates',
  description:
    'How ZZZ Countdown decides what a countdown shows, how quickly corrections are made, and how estimated times are labelled against official announcements.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-12 sm:px-6">
    <p class="text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-secondary dark:text-blue-200">Editorial policy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tighter text-heading md:text-5xl">
      How we update countdown dates
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xl text-muted">
      A countdown page is only worth visiting if the number on it can be trusted. This is the rulebook that keeps that
      true.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 mt-12 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading md:text-3xl">Update triggers</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-lg text-muted">
      <p>
        A page is updated when HoYoverse publishes something, not when a community theory appears. The announcements
        that trigger an update are the pre-download and update notice, the update announcement, the phase channel
        notices, the Intel Report, the store notice and the Special Program post.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a new version is announced, the countdown page, the release time page, the banner page, the pre-download
        page and the content page are rewritten for that version, and the previous version moves to the archive.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 mt-12 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading md:text-3xl">Estimates versus confirmed times</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-lg text-muted">
      <p>
        A time is only presented as confirmed when an official announcement prints it. Everything else is marked as an
        estimate and shows the reasoning. The current example:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-heading">Confirmed:</strong> maintenance starts 2026/10/21 06:00 (UTC+8); Phase I channels close
          2026/11/11 11:59 (server time); Version 3.3 ends 2026/12/02 06:00 (UTC+8).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-heading">Estimated:</strong> the go-live minute at 11:00 (UTC+8), which is the published maintenance
          start plus the “about five hours” HoYoverse estimates; the Phase II banner end, until the Phase II notice is published;
          the next version date, derived from the 42-day cadence.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Estimated times are never presented with a countdown that implies more precision than exists. The estimated card
        is labelled, and the sources page repeats the label.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 mt-12 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading md:text-3xl">How fast we update</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-lg text-muted">
      <p>
        Announcements are read on the day they are published, and the countdown targets are updated the same day. The
        sources page records the last time each announcement was checked, so a reader can tell how current the data is
        without asking.
      </p>
      <p>
        When the maintenance window passes, the status strip on the home page follows the schedule automatically, and
        the “last checked” timestamp is updated by hand whenever the page is reviewed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 mt-12 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading md:text-3xl">Corrections</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-lg text-muted">
      <p>
        A wrong date is corrected as soon as an official source contradicts it, and the change is recorded in the
        verification log. Corrections are not silently overwritten: the log keeps the old value visible next to the new
        one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pb-4 mt-10 sm:px-6">
    <Note
      variant="info"
      title="Questions about this policy"
      description="The contact page explains how to reach the site about a date, a source or a correction."
    />
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm hover:opacity-90"
        href="/contact"
      >
        Contact and corrections
      </a>
      <a
        class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-heading hover:bg-gray-50 dark:border-slate-700 dark:hover:bg-slate-800"
        href="/sources"
      >
        Sources and verification log
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
